{
 "segments": [
  {
   "text": "Case Twenty-Two.",
   "start": 0.75,
   "end": 1.945,
   "pause": 0.6
  },
  {
   "text": "The Honest Fishermen.",
   "start": 2.545,
   "end": 3.803,
   "pause": 1.4
  },
  {
   "text": "In Tidewhistle Cove they say there are two kinds of fishermen. There are honest ones, who tell the truth every time they open their mouths. And there are fibbers, who never tell the truth at all, not even about the weather. Every fisherman is one or the other, and nobody changes from one to the other.",
   "start": 5.203,
   "end": 23.55,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Captain Quill's brand new fishing net had vanished from the harbour wall, and he was sure that one of three fishermen had taken it: Ned, Bran or Col. Exactly one of them took it.",
   "start": 24.4,
   "end": 35.664,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Agnes Bell brought out a plate of saffron buns and asked each of them what they knew. She did not know which of them were honest and which were fibbers. There might be several fibbers, or just one, or none at all.",
   "start": 36.514,
   "end": 49.015,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Ned said, \"I didn't take the net. And Bran is a fibber.\"",
   "start": 49.865,
   "end": 53.236,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Bran said, \"Col took the net.\"",
   "start": 54.086,
   "end": 56.027,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Col said, \"Ned is an honest man. And I didn't take the net.\"",
   "start": 56.877,
   "end": 60.675,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Agnes ate a whole saffron bun very slowly while she thought.",
   "start": 61.525,
   "end": 65.194,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Here are the statements again. Ned: I didn't take it, and Bran is a fibber. Bran: Col took it. Col: Ned is honest, and I didn't take it. Each fisherman is either honest, so everything he says is true, or a fibber, so everything he says is false.",
   "start": 66.044,
   "end": 82.428,
   "pause": 1.1
  },
  {
   "text": "Can you solve it? Who took Captain Quill's net?",
   "start": 83.528,
   "end": 86.195,
   "pause": 1.2
  },
  {
   "text": "Think about it.",
   "start": 87.395,
   "end": 88.419,
   "pause": 0.9
  },
  {
   "text": "Take a moment, or pause here if you are listening. When you are ready, the solution follows.",
   "start": 89.319,
   "end": 94.545,
   "pause": 4.5
  },
  {
   "text": "The Solution.",
   "start": 99.045,
   "end": 100.069,
   "pause": 1.1
  },
  {
   "text": "Bran took the net.",
   "start": 101.169,
   "end": 102.385,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Start with Col. If Col were a fibber, both of his statements would be false. Then Ned would be a fibber, and Col would have taken the net. But if Ned were a fibber, his statement I didn't take the net would be false, which means Ned took it. Both Ned and Col can't have taken the net, so Col is not a fibber. Col is honest.",
   "start": 103.235,
   "end": 122.883,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Since Col is honest, Ned is an honest man and Col didn't take the net. Since Ned is honest, Ned didn't take the net, and Bran is a fibber.",
   "start": 123.733,
   "end": 132.544,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Bran is a fibber, so his statement Col took the net is false, which fits with what we already know. That leaves only one person who could have taken the net: Bran himself.",
   "start": 133.394,
   "end": 144.039,
   "pause": 0.85
  },
  {
   "text": "Bran had borrowed the net because his own was full of holes, and he had meant to bring it back before the captain noticed. Since he is a fibber, he naturally said it was nothing to do with him. Agnes made him mend his own net on the harbour wall that afternoon, where everyone could see him do it.",
   "start": 144.889,
   "end": 161.743,
   "pause": 0.0
  }
 ],
